<title>USA: TABLE-US NAPM index 52.0 Jan versus 53.8 rvsd Dec.</title>
<headline>TABLE-US NAPM index 52.0 Jan versus 53.8 rvsd Dec.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Purchasing Management (NAPM) said on Monday its index of manufacturing activity fell to 52.0 in January from a revised</p>
<p>53.8 in December. A listing of the main NAPM components</p>
<p>follows:</p>
<p>		  Jan   Dec   Nov   Oct   Sept  Aug   July  June</p>
<p>PMI	     52.0  53.8  52.7  50.2  51.7  52.6  50.2  54.3</p>
<p>Production    58.1  58.5  58.6  56.6  54.1  57.0  52.4  55.4</p>
<p>New Orders    53.5  58.2  55.4  51.6  56.3  55.6  54.0  61.3</p>
<p>Supplier Del  48.5  51.6  51.5  50.7  49.7  52.5  50.9  53.2</p>
<p>Inventories   44.4  44.9  41.8  38.9  44.8  41.6  41.2  42.3</p>
<p>Employment    48.7  47.5  47.5  45.5  46.9  48.2  45.5  49.4</p>
<p>Prices	  51.4  50.8  45.9  47.1  51.2  47.4  44.5  49.0</p>
<p>Export Orders 54.6  56.3  55.8  56.1  56.8  57.2  53.8  53.9</p>
<p>Imports	 51.8  52.7  52.5  53.8  51.8  50.6  53.7  48.6</p>
<p>NOTE: Dec PMI was originally reported at 54.0. Dec</p>
<p>production index was originally reported at 58.6.</p>
<p>((-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660))</p>
